      "title": "Troubleshooting Payment Gateway API Rate Limits and Webhook Failures",
      "content_summary": "Addresses HTTP 429 errors, timeouts, and silent webhook failures caused by rate limit misconfigurations or breaking API contract changes in Payment Gateway v2.",
      "content_body": "When experiencing HTTP 429 errors or upstream timeouts, first verify that the current integration is using the correct API schema version for Payment Gateway v2. Breaking contract changes often manifest as schema mismatches that prevent webhooks from firing or cause malformed request errors. Check the gateway dashboard to ensure your rate limit configuration aligns with the production tier requirements. If the issue persists, perform a schema migration to update legacy endpoints and adjust rate limits accordingly to prevent future throttling."
